<code>assert index>=0 && index<\old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<index; (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null) => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))));</code>

This assert statement ensures that for every valid index up to but not including the specified index, each element at these indices remains unchanged or continues to be null if it was initially null.
--------------------
<code>assert index>=0 && index<\old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<index; (this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) || (\old(this.get(i))==null && this.get(i)==null);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert index>=0 && index<\old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0<=i && i<index; (this.get(i) != null && this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) || (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null);</code>
